We first notice the RHS contains a linear term, and this leads to  $g(x)$  to be linear as well.  Let  $g(x) = Ax+B$  and now substitute this expression into the original functional equation: $A[Ax+B] + B = Ax + B + 2x$ ;

and equating like-terms yields: $A^{2} = A + 2  \Rightarrow  A^{2} - A - 2 = 0 \Rightarrow (A-2)(A+1) = 0 \Rightarrow A = -1, 2$ ;

or  $AB + B = B \Rightarrow AB = 0  \Rightarrow  B = 0$ .

Thus,  $\fbox{g(x) = -x, 2x}$  are the only two such functions.

